  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Ram Lal vs State Of U.P. on 30 October, 2019 Author: Dinesh Kumar Singh Bench: Dinesh Kumar Singh High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad, Lucknow Bench ? Court No. - 13 Case :- Criminal Revision No. - 36 of 2008 Revisionist :- Ram Lal Opposite Party :- State of U.P. Counsel for Revisionist :- Vijay Kumar Tripathi,Raj Kumar Singh,Santosh Srivastava Counsel for Opposite Party :- Govt. Advocate Hon'ble Dinesh Kumar Singh,J. 1.",
    "facts": "The present revision petition has been filed challenging the judgment and order dated 18.01.2008 passed by the Additional Sessions Judge, Court No.5, Barabanki in Criminal Appeal No.77 of 1999. 3. Prosecution story, as per record, is that on 26.09.1986 at around 2:00 P.M., Food Inspector, Y.B. Singh collected a sample of Paan Masala manufactured by Chaurasiya and sons, Masakganj, Lucknow weighting 100 gms each from the grocery shop of the accused after giving purchase price Ram Lal vs State Of U.P. on 30 October, 2019 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/120366653/ 1 of Rs.6/-. 4. Public analyst in his examination found that catechu and peppermint were missing from the sample while those were showing as ingredients of the substance by the manufacturer. On the basis of the report of the public analyst, the revisionist was convicted by the trial Court and the same has been affirmed by the appellate court.",
    "arguments": "5. Learned counsel for the revisionist, Mr. Santosh Srivastava submits that the case is of the year 1986. The revisionist had a Kirana shop and he was not the manufacturer of pan masala. He was only a retailer where he sold many grocery items including pan masala. He further submits that the revisionist has already undergone three months imprisonment and he is ready and willing to deposit the fine as directed by the trial Court and affirmed by the appellate Court.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "5. Learned counsel for the revisionist, Mr. Santosh Srivastava submits that the case is of the year 1986. The revisionist had a Kirana shop and he was not the manufacturer of pan masala. He was only a retailer where he sold many grocery items including pan masala. He further submits that the revisionist has already undergone three months imprisonment and he is ready and willing to deposit the fine as directed by the trial Court and affirmed by the appellate Court.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
